  "section": "Movie Facts # 8 of 10",
  "description": "Star Wars was an instant success; within three weeks of the film's release, 20th Century Fox's stock price doubled to a record high. Although the movie's unique cultural neutrality helped it to gain international success, studio exec Alan Ladd Jr. became anxious during the Japanese premiere. The audience responded with silence after the screening, leading many to fear that Star Wars would be unsuccessful in this market. Ladd was soon told that, in Japan, silence was the greatest honor a film could receive. Meanwhile, thousands attended a ceremony at Grauman's Chinese Theater, where C-3PO, R2-D2 and Darth Vader placed their footprints in the movie palace's forecourt."
